# Intuition
<!-- Describe your first thoughts on how to solve this problem. -->
Iterate through each list, always taking the lowest value at any given point.
# Approach
<!-- Describe your approach to solving the problem. -->
I simply ran a while loop until both lists had been fully iterated through.
# Complexity
- Time complexity:
O(n) (where n is the total input size of both lists combined)

# Code Java
```java []
/**
 * Definition for singly-linked list.
 * public class ListNode {
 *     int val;
 *     ListNode next;
 *     ListNode() {}
 *     ListNode(int val) { this.val = val; }
 *     ListNode(int val, ListNode next) { this.val = val; this.next = next; }
 * }
 */
class Solution {
    public ListNode mergeTwoLists(ListNode list1, ListNode list2) {
        /**
        *I create a listnode for the answer,
        *and another listnode that points to the head of 
        *the singly-linked list.
        *This is because I iterate through the list 
        *via answer = answer.next, so I need a pointer to the
        *beginning of the list when I return the answer
        */
        ListNode answer = new ListNode();
        ListNode ans = answer;

        //
        
        while (!(list1 == null && list2 == null)) {
            //If either list is finished, just add the remaining
            //values from the other list
            if (list1 == null) {
                answer.next = new ListNode(list2.val);
                list2 = list2.next;
            }

            else if (list2 == null) {
                answer.next = new ListNode(list1.val);
                list1 = list1.next;
            }

            else {

                if (list2.val < list1.val) {
                    answer.next = new ListNode(list2.val);
                    list2 = list2.next;
                }
                else {
                    answer.next = new ListNode(list1.val);
                    list1 = list1.next;
                }

            }



            answer = answer.next;
            
        }

        return ans.next;
        



    }

    
}
```
